oic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":null,"_gp_pool_share":null,"_score_pool_share":null,"_gate_rev_durability":null,"_gp_rev_durability":null,"_score_rev_durability":0.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.013136262419840646,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":false,"_score_shrhldr_yield":25.7,"_gate_share_shrink":0.053775632050520716,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":0.0,"_gate_sbc_dilution":0.0817823930842144,"_gp_sbc_dilution":false,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.028199999,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":18.8,"_gate_insider_buying":0.0,"_gp_insider_buying":false,"_score_insider_buying":0.0,"pf":[],"description_full":"GCM Grosvenor Inc. is global alternative asset management solutions provider. The firm primarily provides its services to pooled investment vehicles. It also provides its services to investment companies, high net worth individuals, pension and profit sharing plans and state or municipal government entities. The firm invests in equity and alternative investment markets of the United States and internationally. The firm invests in multi-strategy, credit-focused, equity-focused, macro-focused, commodity-focused, and other specialty portfolios. It focuses on hedge fund asset classes, private equity, real estate, and/or infrastructure, credit and absolute return strategies. It also focuses on primary fund investments, secondary fund investments, and co-investments with a focus on buyout, distressed debt, early venture, mid venture, late venture, turnaround, mature, mezzanine, venture capital/growth equity investments. The firm seeks to do seed investments in small, emerging growth, and diverse private equity firms. The firm seeks to make regionally-focused investments in middle-market buyout. It prefers to invest in aerospace and defense, advanced electronics, information technology, biosciences, and advanced materials. It focuses on Europe, Michigan, North Carolina, Colorado, Idaho, Montana, Oregon and Washington. The firm employs fundamental and quantitative analysis. It prefers to have majority stakes in its portfolio companies. GCM Grosvenor Inc. was founded in 1971 and is based in Chicago, Illinois with additional offices across North America, Asia, Australia and Europe. GCM Grosvenor Inc. operates as a subsidiary of Grosvenor Capital Management Holdings, LLLP.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Michael Jay Sacks J.D. | Board Chairman & CEO | Age 62 | Compensation: $6.3M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 550 people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the above the sector median among Financial Services peers, improving at 5%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Each employee generates $318K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $83K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 6\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["GCM Grosvenor Inc. is a small-cap financial services business with a $774M market cap on $558M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +8% over the past three years, a respectable pace for a business of this size. Operating margins are expanding by +6.7pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 19-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $175M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 31 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 4.05\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","Accruals are elevated at -17.0% of assets, and Sloan showed firms building earnings through accruals rather than cash systematically underperform.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 1.4\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage runs at 5.9\u00d7.","Shareholder yield is only 1.3%, a thin return of capital, and insiders hold 2.8% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.8M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Payout ratio of 90% leaves thin coverage if earnings wobble","sev":"amber","cat":"dividend"},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Trading at a 73% margin of safety to estimated fair value \u2014 a real cushion against errors in the estimate","Market is pricing in lower growth than the company has historically delivered","Valued at a 32% discount to sector median EV/EBITDA","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Earnings To Watch: GCM Grosvenor Inc (GCMG) Q3 2026 -- GF Value Sees 10% Upside","source":"finance.yahoo.com","link":"https://finance.yahoo.com/markets/stocks/articles/earnings-watch-gcm-grosvenor-inc-122500257.html","date":"2026-11-06","timestamp":1793967900.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.813,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Exploring Analyst Estimates for GCM Grosvenor (GCMG) Q3 Earnings, Beyond Revenue and EPS","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3024087/exploring-analyst-estimates-for-gcm-grosvenor-gcmg-q3-earnings-beyond-revenue-and-eps?cid=CS-ZC-FT-fundamental_analysis%7Cnfm_preview-3024087","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793884507.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"How (GCMG) Movements Inform Risk Allocation Models","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/15/How_GCMG_Movements_Inform_Risk_Allocation_Models_110126122001_1793553601.html","date":"2026-11-01","timestamp":1793553601.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Reviewing Nuveen Churchill Direct Lending (NYSE:NCDL) & GCM Grosvenor (NASDAQ:GCMG)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/24/reviewing-nuveen-churchill-direct-lending-nysencdl-gcm-grosvenor-nasdaqgcmg.html","date":"2026-10-25","timestamp":1792887297.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.924,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"GCM Grosvenor (NASDAQ:GCMG) vs. Bullish (NYSE:BLSH) Head-To-Head Survey","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/10/10/gcm-grosvenor-nasdaqgcmg-vs-bullish-nyseblsh-head-to-head-sur